// Water-Sector Security Hardening Strategy §5 Tier 2 item 3 follow-up
// (2026-08-01) — real bug found by the first-ever CI run (once GitHub
// Actions was actually enabled on this repo, TD-49): `az bicep build` and
// PSRule both failed on entra/{customers,partners,staff}.bicep with "Error
// BCP204: Extension \"microsoftGraphV1\" is not recognized". Root cause: no
// bicepconfig.json existed ANYWHERE in this tree, so the compiler had
// nothing telling it what the `extension microsoftGraphV1` statement in
// those three files actually refers to — meaning those files may never
// have compiled successfully since they were written on 2026-07-31, since
// nothing ever actually ran `az bicep build` against them for real until
// CI started working today.
//
// No `experimentalFeaturesEnabled.extensibility` flag needed — verified via
// Azure/bicep's own release notes that the experimental flag was REMOVED
// (the feature went GA) in Bicep v0.36.1, and the runner here uses 0.45.15,
// well past that. Matches the official Microsoft Graph Bicep quickstart
// template's own bicepconfig.json exactly
// (github.com/microsoftgraph/msgraph-bicep-types), not an assumption.
//
// Placed at infra-azure/bicepconfig.json, not repo root or inside entra/ —
// Bicep discovers the nearest config by walking up from the target file's
// directory, and this location covers both infra-azure/entra/*.bicep
// (which need it) and infra-azure/main.bicep + modules/*.bicep (which don't
// use the extension but are unaffected by it being available).
{
  "extensions": {
    "microsoftGraphV1": "br:mcr.microsoft.com/bicep/extensions/microsoftgraph/v1.0:1.0.0"
  }
}
